    'The buttons carry a one-time token, not the job’s record ID. In Make, a search that matches nothing returns no bundle and ends its route, so Find the job uses Airtable’s Make an API call instead: it always returns one bundle with a records list, and the router counts it. A second click, a forwarded email or a made-up link finds no job Awaiting owner, and the owner is told it has an answer already.',
